-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  System.Windows.SDK.adam - the Windows SDK's own declarations, each once
  (AD.5a), with no code and no `external`: the Win32 constants and records
  System.Windows and the Windows platform units use, winnt.h's PE / COFF,
  winuser.h's RT_* and winver.h's VS_* / VOS_* / VFT_* that Adam's COFF part
  writes and reads, and the C runtime's lowio and stat names (ucrt's fcntl.h,
  share.h, sys/stat.h) System.HookIO.Win64 hooks.

  Declarations only, so any host imports it: a linux adam writes PE files
  with these names and links nothing of Windows'. System.Windows imports it
  (its routines take these records); a unit that needs only the names
  imports this one alone.
*******************************************************************************/

module unit System.Windows.SDK;

public const
